7. (Original) The method according to claim 6, wherein the obtaining the center-of-mass motion data adjustment value according to the difference between the actual center-of-mass motion data and the reference center-of-mass motion data comprises:

calculating a difference between the actual center-of-mass motion data and the reference center-of-mass motion data; and

obtaining the center-of-mass motion data adjustment value according to a gain matrix and the difference, the gain matrix corresponding to the motion data associated with the center of mass of the robot.



8. (Original) The method according to claim 6, wherein the center-of-mass motion data adjustment value comprises a center-of-mass acceleration adjustment value and a center-of- mass angular acceleration adjustment value.

